4:["$","main",null,{"className":"blog-page","children":[["$","$Le",null,{}],["$","article",null,{"className":"blog-article","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell blog-article-shell","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"className":"blog-back-link","href":"/blog","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":16}]," All guides"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-tag","children":["Admissions"," · ","One Window archive"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Top 5 Universities of Canadato Complete Your Masters"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-article-intro","children":"Canadian universities have traditionally had a strong reputation for both teaching and research. Have you seen what they’re doing in terms of telecom and cyber research? Foreign schools and institutes highly regard the top universities in Canada. These top universities in Canada continue to attract the best and brightest students to their distinguished degree programs. All of these top-ranked colleges, universities, law schools, medical schools, and engineering institutions have a worldwide reputation and continue to be the most popular universities among international students. If you want to study at some of the greatest universities in the world for your Master’s degree, Canada is the place to go. It has the highest rankings and the best reputation. We at OneWindow"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-article-body","children":[["$","section","The guide",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The guide"}],[["$","p","have curated the ” Top 5 universities in Canada ” that you must look for to seek admission in.",{"children":"have curated the ” Top 5 universities in Canada ” that you must look for to seek admission in."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}],["$","section","Cost to study in top universities in Canada",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Cost to study in top universities in Canada"}],[["$","p","International students must assess their financial budgets before beginning the process because of the expenditures associated with studying abroad. The cost of pursuing an MS in Canada comprises one-time pre-arrival fees, tuition fees, and living expenses.",{"children":"International students must assess their financial budgets before beginning the process because of the expenditures associated with studying abroad. The cost of pursuing an MS in Canada comprises one-time pre-arrival fees, tuition fees, and living expenses."}],["$","p","The average annual tuition charge for graduate",{"children":"The average annual tuition charge for graduate"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}],["$","section","education in Canada",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"education in Canada"}],[["$","p","is between 20,000 and 30,000 CAD. The cost of a master’s degree in a Canadian university ranges from 11.11 lakhs to 16.6 lakhs INR for Indian students.",{"children":"is between 20,000 and 30,000 CAD. The cost of a master’s degree in a Canadian university ranges from 11.11 lakhs to 16.6 lakhs INR for Indian students."}],["$","p","The cost of living in Canada is around 2% lower than in the United States. A few states, on the other hand, may have substantially lower costs. The average monthly accommodation expense is between 850 and 1,000 Canadian dollars per year.",{"children":"The cost of living in Canada is around 2% lower than in the United States. A few states, on the other hand, may have substantially lower costs. The average monthly accommodation expense is between 850 and 1,000 Canadian dollars per year."}],"$L11","$L12","$L13"],"$L14"]}],"$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19"]}],"$L1a"]}]}],"$L1b"]}]
